WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.640
- There are many myths about consulting.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.590
One example of things I frequently hear

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:07.140
is that often in consulting projects,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.190
the result is already decided

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.150
at the beginning of the project,

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.190
meaning the consultant
just write down the things

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.620
that the management of
the client is wanting them

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.130
to drive down anyway.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.650
Is all of this true?

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.360
These are the things
that I'm going to discuss

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.480
in this video today.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.500
I'm reviewing the three most common myths

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.840
that I frequently heard about consulting.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.130
So when it comes to another
video here on my channel

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.800
Firm Learning today, it's
quite warm here Munich,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.320
so I'm not drinking a
coffee, but just a water.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.510
Hope that's fine for
you as well as you know,

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.420
my name is Heinrich, on my
channel I want to help you

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.070
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.500
But now without further ado,

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.410
let's jump into the three
myths and let's have a look,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.950
whether these are actually true or not.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.020
So let's start with myth
number one about consulting.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.360
And this is likely the thing
that I hear most frequently

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.960
when people talk badly about consultants.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.810
And this is that
consultants just write down

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.890
what other people on the
client side tell them

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.310
to write down anyway.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.620
So pretty much implying that
the results of the project

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.090
are already clear, already defined

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.930
from the beginning of the project

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.400
and consultants are just
there to make it look good

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.010
just to provide justification
for maybe some harsh measures

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.030
that the management wants to take anyway.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.300
And what these people
mean is that sometimes

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.990
there is senior management
may be off a client.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.930
This senior management wants
to do some harsh measures

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.270
with the organization.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.730
Often this will be
related to cost cutting,

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.550
maybe even deciding to
let go of employees,

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.370
off people in the organization.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.320
And they don't want to
do that on themselves.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.170
They just ask consultants to come in

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.250
and just to do a project,
to investigate these things.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.490
And then in the end, just to write down

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.630
what they wanted to do in the first place.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.170
So what is my view on that?

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.530
And in general, personally,

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.880
I consider this perspective to be fraud.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.360
I never experienced a situation

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.030
where at the beginning of a project,

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.220
it was clear what the
result was supposed to be.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.540
I never was in a meeting with a partner

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.660
or any other senior personnel
of a consulting firm

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.950
telling the team, explaining to the team

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.610
that this is now the task.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.850
This is what we need to
write on a piece of paper.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.280
This is what the client wants.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.540
Of course, that being said,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.980
sometimes you find yourself in a situation

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.900
where the client already
has a couple of hypothesis

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.140
that the client shares with you.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.660
So for instance, yes, it might
be that the client is looking

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.240
into cost cutting measures and
is asking you as a consultant

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.350
to evaluate these cost cutting measures.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.090
And then of course, depending
on the agreed scope,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.950
the result of that might be
that then you as a consultant

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.430
also propose things.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.450
But in my perspective, this
is something very different

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.850
than just writing down what

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.620
the client tells you in the beginning.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.740
Of course, you're going
to pick up some ideas

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.010
that the clients has.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.680
Of course you will evaluate them,

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.850
potentially also incorporate
them in your final suggestion.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.050
Then what is important
to understand is that

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.670
if a consulting firm
delivers a recommendation

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.503
to the client.

00:03:02.503 --> 00:03:04.100
And this is of course, especially true

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.700
for MBB consulting firms
like McKinsey, BCG, or Bain.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.010
The reputation of your firm
will be very much attached

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.580
to the quality of these recommendations.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.870
Just as an example, I in
the past worked for a client

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.260
for a firm and several years ago,

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.140
they apparently did a project
with Boston Consulting Group,

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.470
with BCG and BCG developed
a strategy for this client.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.600
And this document was
still being circulated

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.040
through the organization.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.650
So this BCG strategy document,

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.930
and everyone just called the document,

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:40.100
yeah, the BCG document, the BCG strategy.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:43.190
So clearly your name, your reputation

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:47.400
is often very directly tied
to the results of your work

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.830
and clearly big consulting firms,

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.980
just what they'll be able
to justify to themselves,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.570
just to potentially
damage their reputation.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.770
Do things, write things down

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.510
that they do not believe are true,

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.660
that they do not believe
our recommendation only

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:05.570
because any client is
asking them to do that.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.660
This is just not how it works.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.830
Let's talk about the
second consulting myth,

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.120
and this is that consulting

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.760
is nothing as the
glorified temporary work.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:15.830
This would mean that as a consultant,

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.880
you're not really developing
new concepts and strategies

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.523
as an independent party,
but you are and the nothing,

00:04:22.523 --> 00:04:24.920
it's just an extension of the workforce

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.720
for the employer for your client.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.210
So maybe if a client
needs some extra capacity,

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.350
some extra things that need to get done,

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.540
but the client does not
have enough capacity

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.000
to get this done in-house

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.180
this will be then the
scenario where the client

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.170
is asking for consultants,

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.510
just to take them on as temporary
workers to do the things

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.960
that they cannot currently do
in their home organization.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.210
And my perspective on this is,

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.620
well, there might be some truth to that.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.120
Let me come to that in a
moment, what that would be,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.340
I would argue that this is
largely completely exaggerated

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.660
and not really the case.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.980
As a consultant and I'm specially talking

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.670
about MBB consulting firms,
so McKinsey, BCG, and Bain,

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:05.490
you pride yourself of delivering
an independent opinion

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.330
of delivering your analysis,

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.100
your view on the perspective
that you bring to the client.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.860
Indeed in the normal consulting setup,

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.480
you are not directly reporting
to the client in the sense

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.120
that the client will tell
you what you have to do.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.770
Of course the client, we
want to review your work.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.550
We'll discuss this work with you,

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.300
but usually this will not
take the form of the client

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.650
exactly telling you what
the individual steps are

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.990
that they want you to complete.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.790
And for sure, again, let's
discuss the myth number one,

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.180
they will not tell you what
the results of your work

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.070
are supposed to be.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.320
So general, I disagree with this myth

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.711
and this was even something
that was also top of mind

00:05:40.711 --> 00:05:43.440
of many partners I used to work with

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.700
that they always used to say,

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.040
so we don't want to do is just
to be the extended work bench

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.920
of the clients, just to get
some work done, get tasks done

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.120
that at the moment the
client cannot complete.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.400
It should always be a part
of your independent opinion,

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.320
your perspective that
you bring to the table.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.260
Though that being said,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.110
I think there are two perspectives on this

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.250
where maybe you could come
to the conclusion that yes,

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.010
there might be some truth to that.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.320
And the first is that the
things that I talked about

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.770
are very much true for MBB Consulting,

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:14.490
but might be less true for
other consulting firms,

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.300
maybe especially small or
Boutique Consulting Firms.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.960
So while I don't wanna say
that this is usually the case,

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.130
there might be some consulting
firms where your work often

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.660
is indeed rather compare to temporary work

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.050
than to actually providing
an independent opinion.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.343
And the second perspective
of this is that sometimes

00:06:30.343 --> 00:06:33.360
especially in projects
that are already ongoing

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.360
for a long time project, that
got extension after extension,

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.250
after extension, often you are
really coming with the client

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.030
and to really a working
mode an operational mode

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.610
where you do tasks, agree on
next steps, agree on to dos.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.340
So these are the situations
where then sometimes

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.540
the lines get a little bit blurry.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.210
And here also the client just
might like to work with you

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.320
in this setting, because even
though your fees probably

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.180
are not really economical

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.330
to just use you as a
normal employee equivalent

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.040
for them maybe they just don't
have the budget approval,

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.400
not the means not to hire new people.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.240
And it might just be easier for the client

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.640
to continue working with
you as a consultant,

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.580
even though your fees are much higher

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.430
than what they would pay to an employee,

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:18.640
just out of the convenience aspect of it.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.230
So let's look at myth number three,

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:23.950
and this is that consultants
actually don't care

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.150
about their clients.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.120
They just want to make as
much money as possible.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:30.670
They just want to collect
their consulting fees,

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.730
their per diems from the clients,

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:34.750
and whether what they do then is creating

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.610
any actual value at all.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:40.420
They don't even care about
that as long as they get paid.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.420
And I find this way of talking about

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.380
this quite bitter to be honest.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:48.530
So surely consulting firms as
every other firm is a business

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.420
after all we'll need
to think economically,

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.053
but this just means that
consultants don't care about

00:07:54.053 --> 00:07:56.150
their clients and customers.

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.960
This just seems very wrong to me.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.410
And just to illustrate that.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:04.520
So at my former employer,
one of the highest values,

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:07.870
kind of the highest evolution
level of being a consultant

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:11.770
is really to become a trusted
advisor to the clients,

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:14.880
to the senior management, to
the people that you work with.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:17.760
So whenever one of these
people would have a problem,

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.510
a business related issue
they wanted to discuss,

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:24.190
ideally they would think
about you top of their mind

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.730
about a person that
they can sit down with,

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.690
just use you as a sparing partner,

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.630
discuss some topics with
you then potentially

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:34.600
also then start a project
to address certain issues.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:38.120
So surely deeply caring
about your clients,

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:42.070
deeply being concerned about
what really creates value

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.410
at your clients and has a positive impact

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.440
this from my experience,

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.700
from what I have seen
was always at the core

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.580
of every successful partner I worked with.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.880
I'm not even once experienced
a situation where a partner

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.680
or any other senior person
of the consulting firm

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.950
would just barely imply anything like, oh,

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.240
this project probably will not go away,

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.410
but I don't care because
I will make lots of money

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.243
so that's fine.

00:09:09.243 --> 00:09:12.760
I not even once in six
years working consulting

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:14.910
have I heard anything like this.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.520
And again, it's of course
difficult now to speak

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.760
for every single
consulting firm out there.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:23.530
Of course my experiences
are very much influenced

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.700
by the firm that I worked for.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.680
But I would assume that at least

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.290
for the MBB firms, McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.560
this will be the trend.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.680
This is the situation that you will face.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:38.240
And this was also very well
reflected in the culture

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.070
and also the whole incentive systems,

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.600
how you were also evaluated
even as a junior consultant.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.190
So you would always be rewarded
if you were able really

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.640
to come up with good ideas
that really helped the client.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.310
If you came up with something
that really resonated,

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:56.260
had a positive impact that
really satisfied the client

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.510
and made an impact,

00:09:57.510 --> 00:10:00.400
these were the things that
would make you be perceived

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.710
as a strong consultant as a rock star.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.770
And frankly, if you set
up your work in a way

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.080
that you don't care about
your client's success,

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.170
but just about your own success,

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.330
I think this would be very, very difficult

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:13.760
because often just the
truth that these two

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.210
are very closely interlinked.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.750
So the one regularly leads to the other

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:21.200
and the other way around,
which I think great,

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.350
because this just means that
the incentives are aligned.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.400
So what do you think about these
big myths about consulting?

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.840
Do you think they are true?

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.320
What are your reflections on that?

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.430
We'd love to hear your
perspective, in the video comments,

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.570
to know whether you agree
with what I've said or not.

